    {
      "id": "claim_4d88336da9ad45e3817f9ec22df49447",
      "statement": "Peer coordination can use direct callable endpoints or tools, synchronous or asynchronous results, or shared files, databases, repositories, queues, and blackboards; it requires authenticated identities, task and ancestry IDs, idempotency, concurrency control, distributed termination, and cycle detection, with inter-agent failures capable of cascading.",
